  "notes": [
    "Four banks and one office sky lobby, against burj-class-reference's six banks and three. That is the whole shape of the building: fifty-six of its ninety-one populated office floors are one leg from the street, and the transfer accounting -- where a hop is charged to ttdMeanS and lights no landing button -- is exercised over a much smaller share of journeys than the Burj-class tower exercises it over. GitHub issue #430 asks for exactly that contrast.",
    "The shuttle's cars are rated 10.0 m/s and the bank's travel is 446.4 m, which is above elevator-specs.json airPressure.appliesAboveTravelM (300). The cap and the rating are the same number, so nothing binds and no warning is raised -- this bank is at the cap rather than past it, which is the position every supertall shuttle in the shipped set has been in since the airPressure block landed. Buying speed on this bank is what would make the cap bite, and that is a purchase a player can make rather than a figure authored here.",
    "Every car states passengerTransferS, because data/buildings/README.md refuses to default one on a mixed-use building. The shuttle takes the hotel's 1.5 s rather than the offices' 1.2 s on the README's own rule -- where a bank carries more than one population the slower value is chosen. No new reference value is authored.",
    "The stage cannot draw this tower legibly, on docs/12 SS 4.16's measured 35 legible floors at 1280x800 and 40 at 1440x900 against this building's 119. It is in the same position as burj-class-reference and shanghai-class-reference, and GitHub issue #377 owns the remedy."
  ]
